  {
    "label": "770be8a8-209f-5a4a-8f5b-267370ed95fc",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186059655,
        "id": "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e",
        "title": "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "770be8a8-209f-5a4a-8f5b-267370ed95fc",
        ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })=1.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
